(B) A physician who performs or attempts an abortion in an ambulatory surgical facility or other location that is not a hospital and in which a child is born alive shall immediately take the following steps upon the child's birth:

(1) Provide post-birth care to the newborn in accordance with prevailing and acceptable standards of care;

(2) Call for assistance from an emergency medical services provider;

(3) Arrange for the transfer of the newborn to a hospital.

